- agent: agent-c
- branch: agent/c/m4-w4-sdk
- task: TASK-063
- summary: |
    Wired RtiConnection lifecycle (connect / __aenter__ / __aexit__ / close /
    join_federation) and the injectable transport seam. Added new module
    pysdk/rti1516e/_transport.py with a URL -> server registry
    (register_fake / lookup / unregister / clear) so spec tests can route
    memory:// URLs to an in-process FakeRtiServer instead of a real gRPC
    channel. grpc:// URLs raise NotImplementedError pending real-channel
    wiring (TASK-063 follow-up).

    _FederateContextManager.__aenter__ records create_federation +
    join_federation through the transport, allocates a federate handle
    via transport.allocate_handle(), and constructs a Federate with
    (transport, handle, name). __aexit__ records resign_federation
    (suppressing RuntimeError from a closed connection so it can't mask
    an outer exception). Typed exceptions injected via
    canned_responses propagate naturally — the fake's record() raises
    them, the SDK lets them bubble up.

    Extended pysdk/tests/spec/m4/_fakes/fake_rti_server.py to auto-
    register the fake under memory://fake-rti from __init__ so spec
    tests can construct a fake and immediately call
    RtiConnection.connect("memory://fake-rti") with no extra wiring.
- acceptance:
    - pytest pysdk/tests/spec/m4/test_spec_m4_connection_lifecycle.py: 3/3 GREEN
    - mypy --strict pysdk: clean
    - ruff check pysdk: clean
